{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"S5 landed as commit 02f71da097 on main (Gerrit change 1996 PS2; LLM-Review+1, Verified+1). AC evidence (codebase-verified):\n\nAC1 — gen_cli_help.py --check AND gen_cli_reference.py --check both rc=0; the reference now derives every syntax section from ROUTES + committed help bytes. Verified byte-identical --check under Python 3.11/3.12/3.13.15 (drift gate runs the whole matrix). Proof: scripts/gen_cli_reference.py render()/_syntax_sections; tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py::{test_render_documents_every_live_route,test_render_embeds_help_backed_committed_bytes,test_check_mode_clean_against_committed_tree}.\n\nAC2 — INTERCEPT_COMMANDS, ladder_intercepts() source-regex, and the intercept command census are deleted (no INTERCEPT_COMMANDS/ladder_intercepts/argv[0] tokens remain; MUTATION_VERBS confirmation-line record retained, drift-gated vs _CONFIRM_SCOPE). Proof: test_no_curated_census_symbols_remain, test_generator_source_has_no_intercept_regex.\n\nAC3 — overview/argparse/exit-code tests enumerate route classes via derive_policy_sets()+route attributes, not hand-rebuilt _cli policy unions. Proof: tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py::_routable_subcommands, tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py::test_routing_tables_cover_every_known_subcommand, tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py::dispatcher_arms.\n\nAC4 — a clean no-extras wheel renders every approved help form with exact committed bytes, no heavy/store/config side effect. Proof: tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py (4 passed; runs in CI optionality clean-core-wheel lane, green on Verified).\n\nAC5 — full-extra contract resolves every handler/parser/selector ref and validates every capability-to-extra mapping without command execution. Proof: tests/unit/test_cli_registry_full_extra.py (6 passed).\n\nAC6 — editorial examples/rationale are a structurally separate EDITORIAL_PREAMBLE, registry-linted by lint_editorial() (rejects editorial Usage:/option-table authorities and unknown rebar <cmd> spellings); parser artifacts remain authoritative and render() raises on a dirty preamble. Proof: test_editorial_* + test_render_raises_when_editorial_preamble_is_dirty.\n\nAC7 — same repo-local commands run locally and in portable CI: .github/workflows/_optionality.yml runs both generators --check on the lean wheel + the portable distribution pytest; rebar-mcp smoke-tested as a separate entry point asserting a concrete --help observable (exit 0 + 'rebar-mcp' in output). Verified+1 confirms parity in CI.\n\nAdvisories: ADV1 applied (docs/README.md drift-map row now describes the registry-derived reference; docs/README.md appended to file_impact). ADV3 applied (rebar-mcp smoke asserts concrete observable). LLM-Review PS2 advisory (source-grep test) accepted: paired with observable test_no_curated_census_symbols_remain. Note: plan-review re-sign after the file_impact append was blocked by heavy shared tickets-branch churn (verdict was PASS); the close gate does not re-check plan-review."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787317616734271001,"uuid":"88c28227-8680-4882-9f46-1be4bc30137f"}